  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Year-round production and export of Fairtrade seasonal flowers in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through their local subsidiairy in Ethiopia they want to expand their breeding, processing and selling of fresh summer flowers. For this expansion they need to invest in a new production facility on a new venue. The land is going to be leased directly from smallholders or the company is looking for land that was not in the possession of smallholders.This investment and the activities the company is planning to do will have a significant developing impact. Eventually (after 7 years) the project realizes approximately 1.275 jobs of which app. 75 people will be employed on medium or high level positions. Besides that app. 65% of the total employees will be female. Employees will be trained on the job but also on gender issues and reproductive health including HIV. And finally the company aims as much as possible at buying locally which has a positive effect to indirect jobs.</narrative>
  </description>
